  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — JARVIS Vault\n\nThis repo is 99% Obsidian markdown; the actual test-coverage question applies to a small set of first-party scripts. **Current coverage: 0%.** No `package.json`, no test files (`*.test.js`, `__tests__/`), no test runner config, no CI job exercises any script — the only GitHub Actions workflows deploy `index.html` to Pages.\n\nIn-scope first-party code:\n\n| File | Role | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/priority.mjs` | pure scoring/date functions | 97 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/vault.mjs` | vault walker, frontmatter/task parser | 188 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/brief.mjs` | brief business logic | 278 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/slack.mjs` | delivery + state persistence | 164 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/generate.mjs` | CLI entrypoint | 201 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant/dashboard.mjs` | dashboard entrypoint (reuses lib/) | 230 lines |\n| `sample/scripts/external_id.js` | pure hash utility | 29 lines |\n| `scripts/bootstrap_jarvis_os.js` | one-shot scaffold script | 88 lines |\n| `index.html` (inline `<script>`) | ~5,200-line vanilla-JS PWA | huge |\n\nI recommend `node:test` + `node:assert` — built into Node, zero dependencies, works with `.mjs` directly. No `package.json` exists anywhere, so step 0 for any of this is adding one with a `\"test\": \"node --test\"` script per automation folder (or one root one with `--test-reporter`).\n\n---\n\n### 1. `lib/priority.mjs` — pure functions, highest ROI, zero excuse not to test\n\n**Untested / edge cases:**\n- `urgencyScore`: no `prazo` → 0; boundary values at exactly 3/7/30 days; a past-due `prazo` (falls into the `p <= t` branch, same as \"due today\" — worth locking explicitly).\n- `energyBonus`: unrecognized/undefined value silently → 0 (typo `\"alta\"` gets no bonus — is that intended?).\n- `isBlocked`: `dependencia` as empty array vs. empty string vs. `null` — three different falsy shapes, only two are tested by anyone right now (none, actually).\n- `toDate`: malformed string (e.g. `\"2026-7-6\"` without zero-padding) silently produces `NaN` components — no validation, no test documenting this is unsupported input.\n- `todayISO`: reads `new Date()` directly — **no injection seam**, so it can't be tested deterministically without monkey-patching the global `Date`. Worth flagging as a design gap.\n- `compareTasks`: stability when priority AND due are equal; missing `due` sorts last via `\"9999\"` sentinel — undocumented outside this line.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/priority.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport {\n  urgencyScore, energyBonus, projectScore, isBlocked,\n  toDate, addDays, formatDateBR, taskPriorityValue, compareTasks,\n} from \"./lib/priority.mjs\";\n\ndescribe(\"urgencyScore\", () => {\n  test(\"no prazo returns 0\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(null, \"2026-07-06\"), 0);\n  });\n  test(\"prazo today or past returns 12\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-06\", \"2026-07-06\"), 12);\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-01\", \"2026-07-06\"), 12);\n  });\n  test(\"boundary: exactly 3 days out returns 8\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-09\", \"2026-07-06\"), 8);\n  });\n  test(\"boundary: exactly 7 days out returns 5\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-13\", \"2026-07-06\"), 5);\n  });\n  test(\"boundary: exactly 30 days out returns 2\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-08-05\", \"2026-07-06\"), 2);\n  });\n  test(\"beyond 30 days returns 0\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-09-06\", \"2026-07-06\"), 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"energyBonus\", () => {\n  test(\"baixa -> 2, media -> 1, unknown/undefined -> 0\", () => {\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(\"baixa\"), 2);\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(\"media\"), 1);\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(\"alta\"), 0);\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(undefined), 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isBlocked\", () => {\n  test(\"status pausado is always blocked, dependencia ignored\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ status: \"pausado\" }), true);\n  });\n  test(\"empty dependencia array is not blocked\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ dependencia: [] }), false);\n  });\n  test(\"non-empty dependencia array is blocked\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ dependencia: [\"[[X]]\"] }), true);\n  });\n  test(\"empty string dependencia is not blocked\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ dependencia: \"\" }), false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"projectScore\", () => {\n  test(\"defaults importancia/valor_estrategico to 1 when absent\", () => {\n    const score = projectScore({}, \"2026-07-06\");\n    assert.equal(score, 1 * 10 + 0 + 1 * 8 + 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"toDate\", () => {\n  test(\"null/undefined -> null\", () => {\n    assert.equal(toDate(null), null);\n    assert.equal(toDate(undefined), null);\n  });\n  test(\"truncates a full ISO timestamp to the date part\", () => {\n    const d = toDate(\"2026-07-06T10:00:00Z\");\n    assert.equal(d.getFullYear(), 2026);\n    assert.equal(d.getMonth(), 6);\n    assert.equal(d.getDate(), 6);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"addDays / formatDateBR\", () => {\n  test(\"addDays crosses month boundary\", () => {\n    const d = addDays(new Date(2026, 6, 30), 3);\n    assert.equal(d.getMonth(), 7); // agosto\n    assert.equal(d.getDate(), 2);\n  });\n  test(\"formatDateBR pads day/month and returns '' for falsy input\", () => {\n    assert.equal(formatDateBR(\"2026-07-06\"), \"06/07\");\n    assert.equal(formatDateBR(null), \"\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"taskPriorityValue / compareTasks\", () => {\n  test(\"picks the highest priority emoji present in rawLine\", () => {\n    assert.equal(taskPriorityValue({ rawLine: \"- [ ] foo 🔼 bar 🔺\" }), 4);\n  });\n  test(\"missing rawLine treated as no priority\", () => {\n    assert.equal(taskPriorityValue({}), 0);\n  });\n  test(\"sorts by priority desc, then by due date asc, missing due last\", () => {\n    const a = { rawLine: \"🔼\", due: \"2026-07-10\" };\n    const b = { rawLine: \"🔺\", due: \"2026-07-20\" };\n    const c = { rawLine: \"\", due: null };\n    const sorted = [a, b, c].sort(compareTasks);\n    assert.deepEqual(sorted, [b, a, c]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `lib/vault.mjs` — needs fixture-based integration tests (real fs, temp dir)\n\n**Gaps:**\n- The CRLF→LF normalization (`vault.mjs:42`) is a documented **past production bug** (\"toda nota CRLF era lida como 'sem tipo'\") with **no regression test** — this is the single highest-priority gap in the repo.\n- No cycle/symlink protection in `walkMd` — a symlink loop would hang the walker; untested.\n- `parseFrontmatter`: malformed frontmatter (opening `---\\n` present but no closing `\\n---\\n`) silently treats the *entire file* as body — untested, and arguably wrong behavior for a note with a stray `---` line.\n- `parseSimpleYaml`: no support for YAML block scalars (`|`, `>`) or nested maps — scope boundary undocumented by tests, so future frontmatter additions could silently corrupt data with no signal.\n- `extractTasks`: task regex is anchored at line start (`^-\\s+\\[...\\]`) — **indented/nested checklist items are silently dropped**, no test locks this known limitation.\n- `isRecurringStale`: task with `🔁` and no `due` → stale; `due` in the future → not stale — untested boundary.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/vault.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe, before, after } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { loadVault, extractTasks, isRecurringStale } from \"./lib/vault.mjs\";\n\ndescribe(\"loadVault\", () => {\n  let vaultDir;\n  before(() => {\n    vaultDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-vault-\"));\n  });\n  after(() => fs.rmSync(vaultDir, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n\n  test(\"regression: CRLF-terminated notes still parse frontmatter (past prod bug)\", () => {\n    const content = \"---\\r\\ntipo: projeto\\r\\nstatus: ativo\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n- [ ] foo 📅 2026-07-06\\r\\n\";\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"crlf-note.md\"), content);\n    const { notes, tasks } = loadVault(vaultDir);\n    const note = notes.find((n) => n.fileName === \"crlf-note.md\");\n    assert.equal(note.tipo, \"projeto\");\n    assert.equal(tasks.length, 1);\n  });\n\n  test(\"skips 70 Sistema/Templates, 90 Arquivo, .obsidian, .claude\", () => {\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"70 Sistema\", \"Templates\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"70 Sistema\", \"Templates\", \"t.md\"), \"---\\ntipo: template\\n---\\n\");\n    const { notes } = loadVault(vaultDir);\n    assert.ok(!notes.some((n) => n.fileName === \"t.md\"));\n  });\n\n  test(\"malformed frontmatter (no closing ---) treats whole file as body\", () => {\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"broken.md\"), \"---\\ntipo: projeto\\nsem fechamento\\n\");\n    const { notes } = loadVault(vaultDir);\n    const note = notes.find((n) => n.fileName === \"broken.md\");\n    assert.equal(note.tipo, undefined); // documents current (possibly undesired) behavior\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"extractTasks\", () => {\n  test(\"parses due/scheduled/completed dates and strips emoji from text\", () => {\n    const body = \"- [ ] Ligar cliente 🔺 📅 2026-07-06 ⏳ 2026-07-05\";\n    const [task] = extractTasks(body, { path: \"x.md\", basename: \"x\" });\n    assert.equal(task.due, \"2026-07-06\");\n    assert.equal(task.scheduled, \"2026-07-05\");\n    assert.equal(task.text, \"Ligar cliente\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"ignores task-like lines inside fenced code blocks\", () => {\n    const body = \"```\\n- [ ] not a real task\\n```\\n- [ ] real task 📅 2026-07-06\";\n    const tasks = extractTasks(body, { path: \"x.md\", basename: \"x\" });\n    assert.equal(tasks.length, 1);\n    assert.equal(tasks[0].text, \"real task\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"KNOWN GAP: indented sub-tasks are not matched (documents current limitation)\", () => {\n    const body = \"  - [ ] indented sub-task 📅 2026-07-06\";\n    const tasks = extractTasks(body, { path: \"x.md\", basename: \"x\" });\n    assert.equal(tasks.length, 0); // if this ever becomes 1, update cleanTaskText assumptions elsewhere\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isRecurringStale\", () => {\n  test(\"recurring task with no due date is always stale\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"🔁 every week\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), true);\n  });\n  test(\"recurring task due in the future is not stale\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"🔁\", due: \"2026-08-01\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), false);\n  });\n  test(\"non-recurring task is never flagged stale\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"no recurrence\", due: \"2026-01-01\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. `lib/brief.mjs` — business logic, currently the least-guarded high-value code\n\n**Gaps:**\n- No test that `selectTop3` correctly caps at 3 when more are eligible, or that today-due tasks rank ahead of older overdue ones regardless of `compareTasks` priority.\n- `collectCommercial`: the `RevenueRiskDetected` condition (status ativo + `proximo_contato` overdue) and the \"pipeline value ≥ 10000 with contact in ≤3 days\" condition can **both fire for the same client** — whether they produce a duplicate line (deduped only by exact text match) is untested and looks like a real bug surface.\n- `collectToday`: dedup is scoped only to tasks (`seenToday` set), not across `reuniao` entries — a meeting and a task with identical text would both appear.\n- No test for `buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks: [] })` (empty vault) producing the \"nothing to report\" placeholder text in every section.\n- No test documents behavior when `notes`/`tasks` are `undefined` (throws immediately — an implicit contract with `generate.mjs`'s vault-load error path that nothing verifies).\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/brief.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { buildMorningBrief } from \"./lib/brief.mjs\";\n\nconst TODAY = \"2026-07-06\";\n\ndescribe(\"buildMorningBrief — empty vault\", () => {\n  test(\"renders all placeholder sections with zero notes/tasks\", () => {\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.top3.length, 0);\n    assert.match(brief.text, /nenhuma ação crítica/);\n    assert.match(brief.text, /nada travado/);\n    assert.match(brief.text, /agenda livre/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"selectTop3\", () => {\n  test(\"caps at 3 and ranks today-due tasks ahead of older overdue ones\", () => {\n    const tasks = [\n      { done: false, due: \"2026-06-01\", text: \"old overdue\", rawLine: \"\" },\n      { done: false, due: TODAY, text: \"today A\", rawLine: \"\" },\n      { done: false, due: TODAY, text: \"today B\", rawLine: \"\" },\n      { done: false, due: TODAY, text: \"today C\", rawLine: \"\" },\n    ];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.top3.length, 3);\n    assert.ok(brief.top3.every((t) => t.due === TODAY));\n  });\n\n  test(\"excludes recurring-stale tasks from top3\", () => {\n    const tasks = [{ done: false, due: \"2026-06-01\", text: \"stale recurring\", rawLine: \"🔁\" }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.top3.length, 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"collectCommercial — overlapping conditions\", () => {\n  test(\"KNOWN GAP: client hitting both overdue-followup AND high-value-risk rules — verify no silent duplicate/loss\", () => {\n    const notes = [{\n      tipo: \"cliente\", basename: \"ClienteX\", status: \"ativo\",\n      proximo_contato: \"2026-07-04\", // already overdue\n      valor: 15000,\n    }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes, tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n    // Document actual behavior explicitly rather than assuming — currently expect 2 distinct lines\n    // (different text -> dedupeByText doesn't merge them). Update this assertion once desired behavior is decided.\n    assert.ok(brief.commercial.length >= 1);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"collectRisks\", () => {\n  test(\"blocked project produces ProjectBlocked risk with dependency name\", () => {\n    const notes = [{ tipo: \"projeto\", basename: \"ProjA\", status: \"ativo\", dependencia: [\"[[ProjB]]\"] }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes, tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.ok(brief.risks.some((r) => r.kind === \"ProjectBlocked\" && r.text.includes(\"ProjB\")));\n  });\n\n  test(\"habito-sourced overdue tasks are excluded from risks\", () => {\n    const tasks = [{ done: false, due: \"2026-06-01\", text: \"beber agua\", rawLine: \"\", sourceTipo: \"habito\", sourcePath: \"20 Pessoal/Habitos/x.md\" }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.risks.length, 0);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. `lib/slack.mjs` — the biggest error-handling gap; needs `fetch` mocked\n\n**Gaps:**\n- All three transports call the global `fetch` directly with no injection seam — currently **any test here either hits the real network or must monkey-patch `globalThis.fetch`**. Node's `node:test` `mock` module supports this.\n- Non-2xx response handling (`postN8nWebhook`, `postSlackIncomingWebhook`) — untested error path/message format.\n- `postBotMessage`: HTTP 200 but Slack's `{ ok: false, error }` body — untested; this is a real-world Slack API failure mode (invalid channel, missing scope) that would currently surface as a generic thrown message.\n- `postN8nWebhook`'s JSON-parse-failure fallback (`responseBody = { raw: ... }`) — untested branch.\n- `loadPostState` corrupted-JSON → returns `null` (swallowed) — untested; means a corrupted state file silently resets the dedup guard rather than failing loudly.\n- `alreadyPostedToday` truth table (force / date mismatch / posted=false) — untested.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/slack.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe, mock, beforeEach, afterEach } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport {\n  publishToSlack, loadPostState, savePostState, alreadyPostedToday, saveBriefLocally,\n} from \"./lib/slack.mjs\";\n\ndescribe(\"publishToSlack — transport precedence\", () => {\n  afterEach(() => mock.restoreAll());\n\n  test(\"throws when no delivery method configured\", async () => {\n    await assert.rejects(() => publishToSlack(\"text\", {}), /Entrega não configurada/);\n  });\n\n  test(\"prefers n8nWebhookUrl over slackWebhookUrl and bot token\", async () => {\n    const fetchMock = mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({\n      ok: true, json: async () => ({ received: true }),\n    }));\n    const result = await publishToSlack(\"hi\", {\n      n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n.example/webhook\",\n      slackWebhookUrl: \"https://hooks.slack.com/x\",\n      slackBotToken: \"xoxb\", slackChannel: \"#daily\",\n    }, { date: \"2026-07-06\" });\n    assert.equal(result.method, \"n8n\");\n    assert.equal(fetchMock.mock.calls[0].arguments[0], \"https://n8n.example/webhook\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"n8n webhook non-2xx response throws with body text\", async () => {\n    mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({ ok: false, status: 500, text: async () => \"server exploded\" }));\n    await assert.rejects(\n      () => publishToSlack(\"hi\", { n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n.example/webhook\" }, {}),\n      /n8n webhook falhou \\(500\\): server exploded/\n    );\n  });\n\n  test(\"bot token: HTTP 200 but Slack ok:false surfaces the Slack error\", async () => {\n    mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({ ok: true, json: async () => ({ ok: false, error: \"channel_not_found\" }) }));\n    await assert.rejects(\n      () => publishToSlack(\"hi\", { slackBotToken: \"xoxb\", slackChannel: \"#bad\" }, {}),\n      /Slack API falhou: channel_not_found/\n    );\n  });\n\n  test(\"dryRun short-circuits before any fetch call\", async () => {\n    const fetchMock = mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({ ok: true, json: async () => ({}) }));\n    const result = await publishToSlack(\"hi\", { n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n.example/webhook\" }, { dryRun: true });\n    assert.equal(result.dryRun, true);\n    assert.equal(fetchMock.mock.calls.length, 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"state persistence\", () => {\n  let dir;\n  beforeEach(() => { dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-state-\")); });\n  afterEach(() => fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n\n  test(\"loadPostState returns null for corrupted JSON instead of throwing\", () => {\n    const file = path.join(dir, \"state.json\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(file, \"{not valid json\");\n    assert.equal(loadPostState(file), null);\n  });\n\n  test(\"savePostState creates parent directory and round-trips\", () => {\n    const file = path.join(dir, \"nested\", \"state.json\");\n    savePostState(file, { date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true });\n    assert.deepEqual(loadPostState(file), { date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true });\n  });\n\n  test(\"alreadyPostedToday truth table\", () => {\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday(null, \"2026-07-06\", false), false);\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", false), true);\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", true), false); // force\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-05\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", false), false); // stale date\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: false }, \"2026-07-06\", false), false);\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"saveBriefLocally writes to <outputDir>/<date>-morning-brief.txt\", () => {\n  const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-brief-\"));\n  const file = saveBriefLocally(\"hello\", dir, \"2026-07-06\");\n  assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"), \"hello\");\n  fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Integration gaps — `generate.mjs` / `dashboard.mjs` entrypoints\n\nNo test drives either script end-to-end. Highest-value integration gaps:\n\n- **Exit-code contract is undocumented in tests but explicitly called a \"contract\" in a code comment** (`generate.mjs:190-193`): 0 = ok/skipped, 1 = vault inaccessible, 2 = generated-but-not-delivered. If Task Scheduler or any monitoring depends on these codes, nothing currently guards them against regression.\n- Dedup guard across two real invocations (write state file, run again without `--force`, confirm it's skipped) — untested.\n- `config.json` present but malformed JSON → `JSON.parse` throws uncaught inside `loadConfig`, escaping to the top-level `main().catch` → generic exit 1, indistinguishable from a real vault error. Untested and arguably a bug (should probably be its own status).\n- `dashboard.mjs`'s `countInboxPending` state machine (heading detection turns section on/off, case-insensitive match, ignores empty `\"- \"` placeholder) has zero tests despite parsing a hand-written human file (`raw/inbox.md`) — the most error-prone input format in the whole pipeline.\n- No test confirms Morning Brief and EA Dashboard produce **consistent** priority/risk data from the same vault fixture, despite the code comment stating this shared-lib de-dup is intentional (`dashboard.mjs:8-9`) — nothing locks that contract against future drift.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant/dashboard.integration.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe, before, after } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\n\ndescribe(\"dashboard.mjs end-to-end\", () => {\n  let vaultDir;\n  before(() => {\n    vaultDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-e2e-\"));\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"raw\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"raw\", \"inbox.md\"),\n      \"## Capturas pendentes\\n- ideia solta\\n- \\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"proj.md\"),\n      \"---\\ntipo: projeto\\nstatus: ativo\\nprazo: 2026-07-06\\n---\\n\");\n  });\n  after(() => fs.rmSync(vaultDir, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n\n  test(\"--dry-run does not write output/daily_dashboard.md but reports correct inbox count\", () => {\n    const out = execFileSync(\"node\", [\"dashboard.mjs\", \"--dry-run\", \"--print\"], {\n      cwd: path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant\"),\n      env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vaultDir },\n    }).toString();\n    assert.match(out, /1.*captura aguarda/);\n    assert.ok(!fs.existsSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"output\", \"daily_dashboard.md\")));\n  });\n\n  test(\"normal run writes output/daily_dashboard.md and preserves criado on rerun\", () => {\n    execFileSync(\"node\", [\"dashboard.mjs\"], {\n      cwd: path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant\"),\n      env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vaultDir },\n    });\n    const outFile = path.join(vaultDir, \"output\", \"daily_dashboard.md\");\n    assert.ok(fs.existsSync(outFile));\n    const firstCriado = fs.readFileSync(outFile, \"utf8\").match(/criado: (\\S+)/)[1];\n\n    execFileSync(\"node\", [\"dashboard.mjs\"], {\n      cwd: path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant\"),\n      env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vaultDir },\n    });\n    const secondCriado = fs.readFileSync(outFile, \"utf8\").match(/criado: (\\S+)/)[1];\n    assert.equal(firstCriado, secondCriado);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. `external_id.js` — simple pure function, quick win\n\n```js\n// sample/scripts/external_id.test.js\nconst { test, describe } = require(\"node:test\");\nconst assert = require(\"node:assert/strict\");\nconst { generateExternalId } = require(\"./external_id.js\");\n\ndescribe(\"generateExternalId\", () => {\n  test(\"is deterministic for identical inputs\", () => {\n    const a = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    const b = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    assert.equal(a, b);\n  });\n\n  test(\"differs when notePath differs\", () => {\n    const a = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    const b = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/y.md\");\n    assert.notEqual(a, b);\n  });\n\n  test(\"returns exactly 12 hex chars\", () => {\n    const id = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    assert.match(id, /^[0-9a-f]{12}$/);\n  });\n\n  test(\"relative vs. equivalent absolute path resolve to the same id\", () => {\n    const a = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"./notes/x.md\");\n    const b = generateExternalId(\"/repo/notes\", \"x.md\"); // different repoRoot base\n    // documents whether path.resolve normalization makes these equivalent — currently they do NOT\n    // (different repoRoot arg), which is worth confirming isn't a footgun for callers\n    assert.notEqual(a, b);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Lower-priority / flagged but not skeletoned\n- **`index.html`'s ~5,200-line inline app** (event sourcing, IndexedDB, XP economy) — zero test coverage and out of scope for a `node:test` skeleton; needs its own DOM/Playwright-based pass given its size. This is the single largest untested surface in the repo.\n- **`scripts/bootstrap_jarvis_os.js`** — one-shot scaffold script; worth one idempotency test (running it twice against an existing populated vault shouldn't clobber user content) but low priority since it's not part of any recurring pipeline.\n\n### Summary of top 5 gaps by risk\n1. No regression test for the CRLF-parsing bug already shipped and fixed once (`vault.mjs`).\n2. `slack.mjs` has zero test coverage of its error paths, and no dependency-injection seam for `fetch` — the delivery layer is the least trustworthy part of the pipeline.\n3. `generate.mjs`'s documented exit-code contract (0/1/2) is unenforced by any test.\n4. Overlapping business rules in `collectCommercial` (`brief.mjs`) can double-fire for the same client — behavior is currently unverified, possibly a latent bug.\n5. No CI job runs any of this even if tests are added — test infra (`package.json` + `node --test`) needs to exist before coverage can be sustained.\n",
  "parsedOutput": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Test Coverage Analysis — JARVIS Vault",
        "content": "\nThis repo is 99% Obsidian markdown; the actual test-coverage question applies to a small set of first-party scripts. **Current coverage: 0%.** No `package.json`, no test files (`*.test.js`, `__tests__/`), no test runner config, no CI job exercises any script — the only GitHub Actions workflows deploy `index.html` to Pages.\n\nIn-scope first-party code:\n\n| File | Role | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/priority.mjs` | pure scoring/date functions | 97 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/vault.mjs` | vault walker, frontmatter/task parser | 188 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/brief.mjs` | brief business logic | 278 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/slack.mjs` | delivery + state persistence | 164 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/generate.mjs` | CLI entrypoint | 201 lines |\n| `70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant/dashboard.mjs` | dashboard entrypoint (reuses lib/) | 230 lines |\n| `sample/scripts/external_id.js` | pure hash utility | 29 lines |\n| `scripts/bootstrap_jarvis_os.js` | one-shot scaffold script | 88 lines |\n| `index.html` (inline `<script>`) | ~5,200-line vanilla-JS PWA | huge |\n\nI recommend `node:test` + `node:assert` — built into Node, zero dependencies, works with `.mjs` directly. No `package.json` exists anywhere, so step 0 for any of this is adding one with a `\"test\": \"node --test\"` script per automation folder (or one root one with `--test-reporter`).\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "1. `lib/priority.mjs` — pure functions, highest ROI, zero excuse not to test",
        "content": "\n**Untested / edge cases:**\n- `urgencyScore`: no `prazo` → 0; boundary values at exactly 3/7/30 days; a past-due `prazo` (falls into the `p <= t` branch, same as \"due today\" — worth locking explicitly).\n- `energyBonus`: unrecognized/undefined value silently → 0 (typo `\"alta\"` gets no bonus — is that intended?).\n- `isBlocked`: `dependencia` as empty array vs. empty string vs. `null` — three different falsy shapes, only two are tested by anyone right now (none, actually).\n- `toDate`: malformed string (e.g. `\"2026-7-6\"` without zero-padding) silently produces `NaN` components — no validation, no test documenting this is unsupported input.\n- `todayISO`: reads `new Date()` directly — **no injection seam**, so it can't be tested deterministically without monkey-patching the global `Date`. Worth flagging as a design gap.\n- `compareTasks`: stability when priority AND due are equal; missing `due` sorts last via `\"9999\"` sentinel — undocumented outside this line.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/priority.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport {\n  urgencyScore, energyBonus, projectScore, isBlocked,\n  toDate, addDays, formatDateBR, taskPriorityValue, compareTasks,\n} from \"./lib/priority.mjs\";\n\ndescribe(\"urgencyScore\", () => {\n  test(\"no prazo returns 0\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(null, \"2026-07-06\"), 0);\n  });\n  test(\"prazo today or past returns 12\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-06\", \"2026-07-06\"), 12);\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-01\", \"2026-07-06\"), 12);\n  });\n  test(\"boundary: exactly 3 days out returns 8\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-09\", \"2026-07-06\"), 8);\n  });\n  test(\"boundary: exactly 7 days out returns 5\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-07-13\", \"2026-07-06\"), 5);\n  });\n  test(\"boundary: exactly 30 days out returns 2\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-08-05\", \"2026-07-06\"), 2);\n  });\n  test(\"beyond 30 days returns 0\", () => {\n    assert.equal(urgencyScore(\"2026-09-06\", \"2026-07-06\"), 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"energyBonus\", () => {\n  test(\"baixa -> 2, media -> 1, unknown/undefined -> 0\", () => {\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(\"baixa\"), 2);\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(\"media\"), 1);\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(\"alta\"), 0);\n    assert.equal(energyBonus(undefined), 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isBlocked\", () => {\n  test(\"status pausado is always blocked, dependencia ignored\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ status: \"pausado\" }), true);\n  });\n  test(\"empty dependencia array is not blocked\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ dependencia: [] }), false);\n  });\n  test(\"non-empty dependencia array is blocked\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ dependencia: [\"[[X]]\"] }), true);\n  });\n  test(\"empty string dependencia is not blocked\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isBlocked({ dependencia: \"\" }), false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"projectScore\", () => {\n  test(\"defaults importancia/valor_estrategico to 1 when absent\", () => {\n    const score = projectScore({}, \"2026-07-06\");\n    assert.equal(score, 1 * 10 + 0 + 1 * 8 + 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"toDate\", () => {\n  test(\"null/undefined -> null\", () => {\n    assert.equal(toDate(null), null);\n    assert.equal(toDate(undefined), null);\n  });\n  test(\"truncates a full ISO timestamp to the date part\", () => {\n    const d = toDate(\"2026-07-06T10:00:00Z\");\n    assert.equal(d.getFullYear(), 2026);\n    assert.equal(d.getMonth(), 6);\n    assert.equal(d.getDate(), 6);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"addDays / formatDateBR\", () => {\n  test(\"addDays crosses month boundary\", () => {\n    const d = addDays(new Date(2026, 6, 30), 3);\n    assert.equal(d.getMonth(), 7); // agosto\n    assert.equal(d.getDate(), 2);\n  });\n  test(\"formatDateBR pads day/month and returns '' for falsy input\", () => {\n    assert.equal(formatDateBR(\"2026-07-06\"), \"06/07\");\n    assert.equal(formatDateBR(null), \"\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"taskPriorityValue / compareTasks\", () => {\n  test(\"picks the highest priority emoji present in rawLine\", () => {\n    assert.equal(taskPriorityValue({ rawLine: \"- [ ] foo 🔼 bar 🔺\" }), 4);\n  });\n  test(\"missing rawLine treated as no priority\", () => {\n    assert.equal(taskPriorityValue({}), 0);\n  });\n  test(\"sorts by priority desc, then by due date asc, missing due last\", () => {\n    const a = { rawLine: \"🔼\", due: \"2026-07-10\" };\n    const b = { rawLine: \"🔺\", due: \"2026-07-20\" };\n    const c = { rawLine: \"\", due: null };\n    const sorted = [a, b, c].sort(compareTasks);\n    assert.deepEqual(sorted, [b, a, c]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "2. `lib/vault.mjs` — needs fixture-based integration tests (real fs, temp dir)",
        "content": "\n**Gaps:**\n- The CRLF→LF normalization (`vault.mjs:42`) is a documented **past production bug** (\"toda nota CRLF era lida como 'sem tipo'\") with **no regression test** — this is the single highest-priority gap in the repo.\n- No cycle/symlink protection in `walkMd` — a symlink loop would hang the walker; untested.\n- `parseFrontmatter`: malformed frontmatter (opening `---\\n` present but no closing `\\n---\\n`) silently treats the *entire file* as body — untested, and arguably wrong behavior for a note with a stray `---` line.\n- `parseSimpleYaml`: no support for YAML block scalars (`|`, `>`) or nested maps — scope boundary undocumented by tests, so future frontmatter additions could silently corrupt data with no signal.\n- `extractTasks`: task regex is anchored at line start (`^-\\s+\\[...\\]`) — **indented/nested checklist items are silently dropped**, no test locks this known limitation.\n- `isRecurringStale`: task with `🔁` and no `due` → stale; `due` in the future → not stale — untested boundary.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/vault.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe, before, after } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { loadVault, extractTasks, isRecurringStale } from \"./lib/vault.mjs\";\n\ndescribe(\"loadVault\", () => {\n  let vaultDir;\n  before(() => {\n    vaultDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-vault-\"));\n  });\n  after(() => fs.rmSync(vaultDir, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n\n  test(\"regression: CRLF-terminated notes still parse frontmatter (past prod bug)\", () => {\n    const content = \"---\\r\\ntipo: projeto\\r\\nstatus: ativo\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n- [ ] foo 📅 2026-07-06\\r\\n\";\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"crlf-note.md\"), content);\n    const { notes, tasks } = loadVault(vaultDir);\n    const note = notes.find((n) => n.fileName === \"crlf-note.md\");\n    assert.equal(note.tipo, \"projeto\");\n    assert.equal(tasks.length, 1);\n  });\n\n  test(\"skips 70 Sistema/Templates, 90 Arquivo, .obsidian, .claude\", () => {\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"70 Sistema\", \"Templates\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"70 Sistema\", \"Templates\", \"t.md\"), \"---\\ntipo: template\\n---\\n\");\n    const { notes } = loadVault(vaultDir);\n    assert.ok(!notes.some((n) => n.fileName === \"t.md\"));\n  });\n\n  test(\"malformed frontmatter (no closing ---) treats whole file as body\", () => {\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"broken.md\"), \"---\\ntipo: projeto\\nsem fechamento\\n\");\n    const { notes } = loadVault(vaultDir);\n    const note = notes.find((n) => n.fileName === \"broken.md\");\n    assert.equal(note.tipo, undefined); // documents current (possibly undesired) behavior\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"extractTasks\", () => {\n  test(\"parses due/scheduled/completed dates and strips emoji from text\", () => {\n    const body = \"- [ ] Ligar cliente 🔺 📅 2026-07-06 ⏳ 2026-07-05\";\n    const [task] = extractTasks(body, { path: \"x.md\", basename: \"x\" });\n    assert.equal(task.due, \"2026-07-06\");\n    assert.equal(task.scheduled, \"2026-07-05\");\n    assert.equal(task.text, \"Ligar cliente\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"ignores task-like lines inside fenced code blocks\", () => {\n    const body = \"```\\n- [ ] not a real task\\n```\\n- [ ] real task 📅 2026-07-06\";\n    const tasks = extractTasks(body, { path: \"x.md\", basename: \"x\" });\n    assert.equal(tasks.length, 1);\n    assert.equal(tasks[0].text, \"real task\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"KNOWN GAP: indented sub-tasks are not matched (documents current limitation)\", () => {\n    const body = \"  - [ ] indented sub-task 📅 2026-07-06\";\n    const tasks = extractTasks(body, { path: \"x.md\", basename: \"x\" });\n    assert.equal(tasks.length, 0); // if this ever becomes 1, update cleanTaskText assumptions elsewhere\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isRecurringStale\", () => {\n  test(\"recurring task with no due date is always stale\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"🔁 every week\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), true);\n  });\n  test(\"recurring task due in the future is not stale\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"🔁\", due: \"2026-08-01\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), false);\n  });\n  test(\"non-recurring task is never flagged stale\", () => {\n    assert.equal(isRecurringStale({ rawLine: \"no recurrence\", due: \"2026-01-01\" }, \"2026-07-06\"), false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "3. `lib/brief.mjs` — business logic, currently the least-guarded high-value code",
        "content": "\n**Gaps:**\n- No test that `selectTop3` correctly caps at 3 when more are eligible, or that today-due tasks rank ahead of older overdue ones regardless of `compareTasks` priority.\n- `collectCommercial`: the `RevenueRiskDetected` condition (status ativo + `proximo_contato` overdue) and the \"pipeline value ≥ 10000 with contact in ≤3 days\" condition can **both fire for the same client** — whether they produce a duplicate line (deduped only by exact text match) is untested and looks like a real bug surface.\n- `collectToday`: dedup is scoped only to tasks (`seenToday` set), not across `reuniao` entries — a meeting and a task with identical text would both appear.\n- No test for `buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks: [] })` (empty vault) producing the \"nothing to report\" placeholder text in every section.\n- No test documents behavior when `notes`/`tasks` are `undefined` (throws immediately — an implicit contract with `generate.mjs`'s vault-load error path that nothing verifies).\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/brief.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { buildMorningBrief } from \"./lib/brief.mjs\";\n\nconst TODAY = \"2026-07-06\";\n\ndescribe(\"buildMorningBrief — empty vault\", () => {\n  test(\"renders all placeholder sections with zero notes/tasks\", () => {\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.top3.length, 0);\n    assert.match(brief.text, /nenhuma ação crítica/);\n    assert.match(brief.text, /nada travado/);\n    assert.match(brief.text, /agenda livre/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"selectTop3\", () => {\n  test(\"caps at 3 and ranks today-due tasks ahead of older overdue ones\", () => {\n    const tasks = [\n      { done: false, due: \"2026-06-01\", text: \"old overdue\", rawLine: \"\" },\n      { done: false, due: TODAY, text: \"today A\", rawLine: \"\" },\n      { done: false, due: TODAY, text: \"today B\", rawLine: \"\" },\n      { done: false, due: TODAY, text: \"today C\", rawLine: \"\" },\n    ];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.top3.length, 3);\n    assert.ok(brief.top3.every((t) => t.due === TODAY));\n  });\n\n  test(\"excludes recurring-stale tasks from top3\", () => {\n    const tasks = [{ done: false, due: \"2026-06-01\", text: \"stale recurring\", rawLine: \"🔁\" }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.top3.length, 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"collectCommercial — overlapping conditions\", () => {\n  test(\"KNOWN GAP: client hitting both overdue-followup AND high-value-risk rules — verify no silent duplicate/loss\", () => {\n    const notes = [{\n      tipo: \"cliente\", basename: \"ClienteX\", status: \"ativo\",\n      proximo_contato: \"2026-07-04\", // already overdue\n      valor: 15000,\n    }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes, tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n    // Document actual behavior explicitly rather than assuming — currently expect 2 distinct lines\n    // (different text -> dedupeByText doesn't merge them). Update this assertion once desired behavior is decided.\n    assert.ok(brief.commercial.length >= 1);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"collectRisks\", () => {\n  test(\"blocked project produces ProjectBlocked risk with dependency name\", () => {\n    const notes = [{ tipo: \"projeto\", basename: \"ProjA\", status: \"ativo\", dependencia: [\"[[ProjB]]\"] }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes, tasks: [] }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.ok(brief.risks.some((r) => r.kind === \"ProjectBlocked\" && r.text.includes(\"ProjB\")));\n  });\n\n  test(\"habito-sourced overdue tasks are excluded from risks\", () => {\n    const tasks = [{ done: false, due: \"2026-06-01\", text: \"beber agua\", rawLine: \"\", sourceTipo: \"habito\", sourcePath: \"20 Pessoal/Habitos/x.md\" }];\n    const brief = buildMorningBrief({ notes: [], tasks }, { today: TODAY });\n    assert.equal(brief.risks.length, 0);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "4. `lib/slack.mjs` — the biggest error-handling gap; needs `fetch` mocked",
        "content": "\n**Gaps:**\n- All three transports call the global `fetch` directly with no injection seam — currently **any test here either hits the real network or must monkey-patch `globalThis.fetch`**. Node's `node:test` `mock` module supports this.\n- Non-2xx response handling (`postN8nWebhook`, `postSlackIncomingWebhook`) — untested error path/message format.\n- `postBotMessage`: HTTP 200 but Slack's `{ ok: false, error }` body — untested; this is a real-world Slack API failure mode (invalid channel, missing scope) that would currently surface as a generic thrown message.\n- `postN8nWebhook`'s JSON-parse-failure fallback (`responseBody = { raw: ... }`) — untested branch.\n- `loadPostState` corrupted-JSON → returns `null` (swallowed) — untested; means a corrupted state file silently resets the dedup guard rather than failing loudly.\n- `alreadyPostedToday` truth table (force / date mismatch / posted=false) — untested.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/morning-brief/lib/slack.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe, mock, beforeEach, afterEach } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport {\n  publishToSlack, loadPostState, savePostState, alreadyPostedToday, saveBriefLocally,\n} from \"./lib/slack.mjs\";\n\ndescribe(\"publishToSlack — transport precedence\", () => {\n  afterEach(() => mock.restoreAll());\n\n  test(\"throws when no delivery method configured\", async () => {\n    await assert.rejects(() => publishToSlack(\"text\", {}), /Entrega não configurada/);\n  });\n\n  test(\"prefers n8nWebhookUrl over slackWebhookUrl and bot token\", async () => {\n    const fetchMock = mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({\n      ok: true, json: async () => ({ received: true }),\n    }));\n    const result = await publishToSlack(\"hi\", {\n      n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n.example/webhook\",\n      slackWebhookUrl: \"https://hooks.slack.com/x\",\n      slackBotToken: \"xoxb\", slackChannel: \"#daily\",\n    }, { date: \"2026-07-06\" });\n    assert.equal(result.method, \"n8n\");\n    assert.equal(fetchMock.mock.calls[0].arguments[0], \"https://n8n.example/webhook\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"n8n webhook non-2xx response throws with body text\", async () => {\n    mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({ ok: false, status: 500, text: async () => \"server exploded\" }));\n    await assert.rejects(\n      () => publishToSlack(\"hi\", { n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n.example/webhook\" }, {}),\n      /n8n webhook falhou \\(500\\): server exploded/\n    );\n  });\n\n  test(\"bot token: HTTP 200 but Slack ok:false surfaces the Slack error\", async () => {\n    mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({ ok: true, json: async () => ({ ok: false, error: \"channel_not_found\" }) }));\n    await assert.rejects(\n      () => publishToSlack(\"hi\", { slackBotToken: \"xoxb\", slackChannel: \"#bad\" }, {}),\n      /Slack API falhou: channel_not_found/\n    );\n  });\n\n  test(\"dryRun short-circuits before any fetch call\", async () => {\n    const fetchMock = mock.method(globalThis, \"fetch\", async () => ({ ok: true, json: async () => ({}) }));\n    const result = await publishToSlack(\"hi\", { n8nWebhookUrl: \"https://n8n.example/webhook\" }, { dryRun: true });\n    assert.equal(result.dryRun, true);\n    assert.equal(fetchMock.mock.calls.length, 0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"state persistence\", () => {\n  let dir;\n  beforeEach(() => { dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-state-\")); });\n  afterEach(() => fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n\n  test(\"loadPostState returns null for corrupted JSON instead of throwing\", () => {\n    const file = path.join(dir, \"state.json\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(file, \"{not valid json\");\n    assert.equal(loadPostState(file), null);\n  });\n\n  test(\"savePostState creates parent directory and round-trips\", () => {\n    const file = path.join(dir, \"nested\", \"state.json\");\n    savePostState(file, { date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true });\n    assert.deepEqual(loadPostState(file), { date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true });\n  });\n\n  test(\"alreadyPostedToday truth table\", () => {\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday(null, \"2026-07-06\", false), false);\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", false), true);\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", true), false); // force\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-05\", posted: true }, \"2026-07-06\", false), false); // stale date\n    assert.equal(alreadyPostedToday({ date: \"2026-07-06\", posted: false }, \"2026-07-06\", false), false);\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"saveBriefLocally writes to <outputDir>/<date>-morning-brief.txt\", () => {\n  const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-brief-\"));\n  const file = saveBriefLocally(\"hello\", dir, \"2026-07-06\");\n  assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"), \"hello\");\n  fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. Integration gaps — `generate.mjs` / `dashboard.mjs` entrypoints",
        "content": "\nNo test drives either script end-to-end. Highest-value integration gaps:\n\n- **Exit-code contract is undocumented in tests but explicitly called a \"contract\" in a code comment** (`generate.mjs:190-193`): 0 = ok/skipped, 1 = vault inaccessible, 2 = generated-but-not-delivered. If Task Scheduler or any monitoring depends on these codes, nothing currently guards them against regression.\n- Dedup guard across two real invocations (write state file, run again without `--force`, confirm it's skipped) — untested.\n- `config.json` present but malformed JSON → `JSON.parse` throws uncaught inside `loadConfig`, escaping to the top-level `main().catch` → generic exit 1, indistinguishable from a real vault error. Untested and arguably a bug (should probably be its own status).\n- `dashboard.mjs`'s `countInboxPending` state machine (heading detection turns section on/off, case-insensitive match, ignores empty `\"- \"` placeholder) has zero tests despite parsing a hand-written human file (`raw/inbox.md`) — the most error-prone input format in the whole pipeline.\n- No test confirms Morning Brief and EA Dashboard produce **consistent** priority/risk data from the same vault fixture, despite the code comment stating this shared-lib de-dup is intentional (`dashboard.mjs:8-9`) — nothing locks that contract against future drift.\n\n```js\n// 70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant/dashboard.integration.test.mjs\nimport { test, describe, before, after } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\n\ndescribe(\"dashboard.mjs end-to-end\", () => {\n  let vaultDir;\n  before(() => {\n    vaultDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"jarvis-e2e-\"));\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"raw\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"raw\", \"inbox.md\"),\n      \"## Capturas pendentes\\n- ideia solta\\n- \\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"proj.md\"),\n      \"---\\ntipo: projeto\\nstatus: ativo\\nprazo: 2026-07-06\\n---\\n\");\n  });\n  after(() => fs.rmSync(vaultDir, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n\n  test(\"--dry-run does not write output/daily_dashboard.md but reports correct inbox count\", () => {\n    const out = execFileSync(\"node\", [\"dashboard.mjs\", \"--dry-run\", \"--print\"], {\n      cwd: path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant\"),\n      env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vaultDir },\n    }).toString();\n    assert.match(out, /1.*captura aguarda/);\n    assert.ok(!fs.existsSync(path.join(vaultDir, \"output\", \"daily_dashboard.md\")));\n  });\n\n  test(\"normal run writes output/daily_dashboard.md and preserves criado on rerun\", () => {\n    execFileSync(\"node\", [\"dashboard.mjs\"], {\n      cwd: path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant\"),\n      env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vaultDir },\n    });\n    const outFile = path.join(vaultDir, \"output\", \"daily_dashboard.md\");\n    assert.ok(fs.existsSync(outFile));\n    const firstCriado = fs.readFileSync(outFile, \"utf8\").match(/criado: (\\S+)/)[1];\n\n    execFileSync(\"node\", [\"dashboard.mjs\"], {\n      cwd: path.resolve(\"70 Sistema/Automacao/executive-assistant\"),\n      env: { ...process.env, JARVIS_VAULT_ROOT: vaultDir },\n    });\n    const secondCriado = fs.readFileSync(outFile, \"utf8\").match(/criado: (\\S+)/)[1];\n    assert.equal(firstCriado, secondCriado);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "6. `external_id.js` — simple pure function, quick win",
        "content": "\n```js\n// sample/scripts/external_id.test.js\nconst { test, describe } = require(\"node:test\");\nconst assert = require(\"node:assert/strict\");\nconst { generateExternalId } = require(\"./external_id.js\");\n\ndescribe(\"generateExternalId\", () => {\n  test(\"is deterministic for identical inputs\", () => {\n    const a = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    const b = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    assert.equal(a, b);\n  });\n\n  test(\"differs when notePath differs\", () => {\n    const a = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    const b = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/y.md\");\n    assert.notEqual(a, b);\n  });\n\n  test(\"returns exactly 12 hex chars\", () => {\n    const id = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"notes/x.md\");\n    assert.match(id, /^[0-9a-f]{12}$/);\n  });\n\n  test(\"relative vs. equivalent absolute path resolve to the same id\", () => {\n    const a = generateExternalId(\"/repo\", \"./notes/x.md\");\n    const b = generateExternalId(\"/repo/notes\", \"x.md\"); // different repoRoot base\n    // documents whether path.resolve normalization makes these equivalent — currently they do NOT\n    // (different repoRoot arg), which is worth confirming isn't a footgun for callers\n    assert.notEqual(a, b);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Lower-priority / flagged but not skeletoned",
        "content": "- **`index.html`'s ~5,200-line inline app** (event sourcing, IndexedDB, XP economy) — zero test coverage and out of scope for a `node:test` skeleton; needs its own DOM/Playwright-based pass given its size. This is the single largest untested surface in the repo.\n- **`scripts/bootstrap_jarvis_os.js`** — one-shot scaffold script; worth one idempotency test (running it twice against an existing populated vault shouldn't clobber user content) but low priority since it's not part of any recurring pipeline.\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary of top 5 gaps by risk",
        "content": "1. No regression test for the CRLF-parsing bug already shipped and fixed once (`vault.mjs`).\n2. `slack.mjs` has zero test coverage of its error paths, and no dependency-injection seam for `fetch` — the delivery layer is the least trustworthy part of the pipeline.\n3. `generate.mjs`'s documented exit-code contract (0/1/2) is unenforced by any test.\n4. Overlapping business rules in `collectCommercial` (`brief.mjs`) can double-fire for the same client — behavior is currently unverified, possibly a latent bug.\n5. No CI job runs any of this even if tests are added — test infra (`package.json` + `node --test`) needs to exist before coverage can be sustained.",
        "level": 3
      }
